#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c8e0eb-b4ed-5750-97d5-7df316c93a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513595} {:answer/id #uuid "5109da14-c4b1-5d66-8b72-c7c4fe59acde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513753} {:answer/id #uuid "8e41c8c1-320c-5148-80c5-566550b07342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513899} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8b9732-250a-5c1f-8b41-8e1659261954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514030} {:answer/id #uuid "ccf68bac-d6a7-5572-952f-aca8d66f7daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514062}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513595} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f9929b-cbb7-535e-88cc-fde1a1ddedec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e03bdc50-8826-55ed-961a-7b04fba13b73" :question/math-academy-id "q-43064" :question/problem "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =20+2 \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{22}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1535aac7-a580-50c9-bb4b-02062ef10430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513587} {:answer/id #uuid "30b9adea-211f-53a0-9e3a-0b6f4d8b955e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513661} {:answer/id #uuid "6744b428-41a3-57bb-b1be-72c3c470befb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513808} {:answer/id #uuid "a12728ba-7099-5bf8-8866-47c0e9602d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513945} {:answer/id #uuid "a12f5c16-20dd-5336-876b-869d81a32fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513946}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513587} :answer-field/id #uuid "c336fca6-9149-5cbc-a19d-a2bfb6cf6d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e3cff1af-b64e-5d5d-98b9-281348f5cad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130697" :question/problem "Given that \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}a+5 & 5 \\\\ b & -3\\end{vmatrix}=-34,\n$$\nfind \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}a+4 & 5 \\\\ b+2 & -3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}a+4 & 5 \\\\ b+2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}(a+5)-1 & 5 \\\\ b+2 & -3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}(a+5)-1 & 5 \\\\ b+2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} & =\\underbrace{\\begin{vmatrix}a+5 & 5 \\\\ b & -3\\end{vmatrix}}_{-34}+\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-34+(3-10) \\\\  & =-41.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ebf46d3-5341-5dd3-aceb-6ddffa810768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522188} {:answer/id #uuid "6aad5572-7448-5e77-a728-919195780102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522235} {:answer/id #uuid "9171c738-0ec4-5a88-b47b-0045bdab10e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522317} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b46094-adbe-5613-99fb-1d44ee476d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522431} {:answer/id #uuid "ea933042-3f02-5de2-bb89-d29c596a91bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522520}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522188} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab7f2cb8-335b-5f4a-9cc8-0908a43a3d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "64b1d8f8-0962-5304-966e-2b0899590d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139982" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e0e3711-6463-5725-af73-097d1ae29a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522214} {:answer/id #uuid "61446332-0629-5ef8-8fdd-ddaab16f7297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522220} {:answer/id #uuid "8522d96b-7f5f-51ec-a409-3570be436a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522286} {:answer/id #uuid "8b68a9a3-d2ff-5fe6-a44b-0661eda03baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522303} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e1f722-dade-587d-89a7-857b88b1ecf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522459}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522303} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e4bc43-9fa2-56e5-9887-5f6820f6d33f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "900f650b-6d73-5995-901b-d7a17074a6aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-141232" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $6\\times 10$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10,$ and since $B$ is formed by $4$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0489d7c0-9892-5b4f-a265-35a855cae665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522025} {:answer/id #uuid "19d7b093-ccfa-5074-9a83-a27b17ba1454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522078} {:answer/id #uuid "40c69629-2803-5ad7-aa97-c2b10a5bb2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522158} {:answer/id #uuid "9b640a26-d27a-5063-8ab1-f9eddbf076e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522337} {:answer/id #uuid "f26141c5-5ae9-5b4b-80af-055e70b6a825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522078} :answer-field/id #uuid "70719b4e-2718-5ba2-8435-476dae5ff60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b1b6e064-faca-5061-955a-61c19c8be97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142481" :question/problem "Consider a $4\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f279b3-ea5e-5d31-9dcd-0a3e8e1b3a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522038} {:answer/id #uuid "2c39de95-065d-5909-a31e-8aec18fcaa30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522120} {:answer/id #uuid "5c15ec5b-b014-5f4f-aedd-7a3ee80c6e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522210} {:answer/id #uuid "c65ee4e2-e412-5286-95cc-2961eb9dd28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522434} {:answer/id #uuid "daf23a31-b6e9-551f-8960-6733a9da0c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522038} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7368f2-5a45-59f1-9769-661d58ae07d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c579df31-38e7-5faa-a719-e9a3badf209e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35435" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$ \n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $A$ is not invertible" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}=\\text{Span}\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 4,$ then, by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 4$, according to the  invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "515cb0ad-3bf4-5d0b-b7db-ba6abbf4f45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522193} {:answer/id #uuid "87510f02-5814-56e6-9a0a-3bbbf7e6baba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522288} {:answer/id #uuid "b3fe8edc-cf8c-59b3-845a-0f711614663c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522389} {:answer/id #uuid "e0746fb2-e7e9-54d9-93d0-235af2e3310d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522494} {:answer/id #uuid "e37b3463-8c25-56aa-885e-ca8b85bf4b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522504}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522389} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ade6f1-cb8a-5617-b68c-23062a0a94c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3fc6c03-9e92-5752-b628-3af41a4a428b" :question/math-academy-id "q-139981" :question/problem "Consider a $9\\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=4$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523101 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46fe9d86-8a7b-5b31-9f33-352086d9b0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523118} {:answer/id #uuid "58a2e68c-7ee5-5893-a320-e4d59782d97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523118} :answer-field/id #uuid "072bdae2-59da-58c7-af80-28f3f2f9aae7" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02336600-7104-5fb9-9b31-cae1a52518dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523092} {:answer/id #uuid "547d116e-af59-5ba8-b479-146d79b8a167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523124} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c4297dc-f995-5396-8e9e-d024c65ce177" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141e0203-23b8-5619-a962-5626778a971c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523103} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb4a988-bcd2-5b80-a37e-65bc083843a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523103} :answer-field/id #uuid "60631e67-ec0e-5269-b67b-3fd99562c886" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1080e551-06cd-5714-8bdc-170d1f4b1992" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=0 \\\\ x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e065480-c3c7-5a97-80dd-f851baccc4cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523108} {:answer/id #uuid "63fa15da-a612-551e-bc84-28195f146d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523135} :answer-field/id #uuid "95720269-0a64-5442-8ea6-fada3caa3f3d" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a075d6f9-6a6b-521c-9a45-cefd6406a87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523157} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d89df8-a864-501a-978f-d1b4c908a594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523159}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523157} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f4634b-41cc-5f87-b51b-46f0fed4e546" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c51d359e-c96e-568d-a08a-cc6a5975c003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523169} {:answer/id #uuid "d80969b7-edb9-54aa-9415-47b2ca6fa4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523176}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523176} :answer-field/id #uuid "da426b62-5fc6-56a5-92f1-825ae424ef78" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2c37a8ce-9961-58b3-83eb-74946c8f3663" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=-4 \\\\ x+3y &=-8 \\\\ x+y-4z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is inconsistent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92f5b3ce-9f77-555e-a32f-418bc4e4ae3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523151} {:answer/id #uuid "9552d211-6758-511e-9dd2-695af0b42a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523151} :answer-field/id #uuid "178e2ad7-57e9-5728-a5d6-b6e9f1ddc32e" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1127203c-eb67-5f24-9963-9f6c74e2e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523102} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3c86e8-fe67-5803-979e-32951465e4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523140}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523102} :answer-field/id #uuid "8925e95f-c16a-5da9-bc62-4ffcfe2c9609" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f9e16b-ee78-5f24-a114-9509d560608d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523162} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb07647-4604-59aa-a0cf-ee179bfdcceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523191}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523191} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98057d3-cab1-5021-9e07-c30835639d6d" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "482e6d01-f9bf-525e-86f9-c527dca5de7f" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+6y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent dependent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4094b2ed-2795-574f-9bb3-fb2c83ecb51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523117} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0b8de0-9754-5abb-bbaa-1a2488a781e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523129}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523117} :answer-field/id #uuid "25d63ecc-0162-52f1-8496-c91465d5168f" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523109} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b4a9eea-9608-50ab-9333-020c18e9ce1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523121} {:answer/id #uuid "f60437e2-7dd6-546f-9828-b80e9f59a8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523188}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523121} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ddd758a-c236-567f-9e01-d88d008f82a6" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87d21643-01b3-5b36-833a-4904b0c0d2ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523143} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fe98d8-0f7b-5c9d-87ac-6ff411f4142c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523187} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dc94f57-6ef6-5b16-95f9-1ae9415ced68" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "48bd3d4c-5e94-556e-bb2a-82b8de48db17" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ -2x-y-7z &=-2 \\\\ 2x+11z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 11 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1df67eee-8e7e-5eb7-ba3b-02df7c2b88d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523107} {:answer/id #uuid "edeeea6a-d422-56c3-b686-ec4bc3cfaaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523182}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523182} :answer-field/id #uuid "7506832c-a1c4-534a-b2e6-d51bb3a21471" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f63a9e5-2946-52bc-8fdc-8b775647cf8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523130} {:answer/id #uuid "613155d7-d7de-5a5a-91c3-ac538369b356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523130} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac0ae869-8ade-5317-96c1-5e22aec5b834" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53e8ac69-39e1-5dfb-b044-65b188ea3777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523123} {:answer/id #uuid "912e1233-1f11-5ad2-85d3-0096b74affbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523123} :answer-field/id #uuid "f44f1c65-b30b-551b-a69a-7f4cd3ad8965" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "636c60f0-5dc2-592a-9ada-f299790fa243" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=5 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=7 \\\\ x+3y+5z &=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51be9dbd-7ee6-56c1-a547-5903d2a1b3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523122} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d7767c-aca7-50f4-90dc-f407ea0d7a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523186} :answer-field/id #uuid "996ab691-0a7b-56e9-804a-a2787a923077" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a23b4315-1a65-506a-8c02-738beed7aaa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523158} {:answer/id #uuid "bb33e391-198c-5529-9d5b-397721de092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523164}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523158} :answer-field/id #uuid "d28f612b-3349-546c-9210-2a56396e5c6f" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e08fdf-8af3-5a6d-a236-96fcf159b0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523095} {:answer/id #uuid "60e8b807-93c5-5642-bfc7-4739a9cf92c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523095} :answer-field/id #uuid "f478684b-108b-505b-8b25-f8e1f9defb6d" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8a8ea6cd-37c6-57a9-b6bb-655208ae0dae" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ 2x+5y &=7 \\\\ -2x-3y+5z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b71e9efd-4041-5353-b773-e73d4943b58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523163} {:answer/id #uuid "c040c9e9-b2b2-5290-9279-e6d8a22bf949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523167}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523167} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c161978-1b18-5f69-ab37-c6a064914aa4" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523097} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1070f3b9-edc1-598f-9822-27e3abfa3c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523100} {:answer/id #uuid "86e55745-a3ef-551c-a3b4-ce4d34f0d892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523142}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523100} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a48fbc9-4e49-5abc-8cad-5f489b22b567" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523145} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca331de-6d7a-5bec-913c-999c56c3d275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523098} {:answer/id #uuid "768483dd-8204-52e1-a40b-ab97ef2fad60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523139}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523139} :answer-field/id #uuid "96339ae7-9e2a-597d-b5f3-d761fa172570" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e31a150-29e9-5dea-94ac-a18aad26fe11" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=1 \\\\ 2x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e13df2-cbbc-5122-a312-3d4718cfd2d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523126} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce05a37-3f4d-53ca-9976-cf02a4b3a3bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523147}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523126} :answer-field/id #uuid "2629fa4f-103c-5153-9f74-91ca5c93439c" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523110} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554b6c18-e491-5f95-965d-fa5a2bd9d88d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523125} {:answer/id #uuid "f97645eb-31df-5037-9f30-9be5b18f44ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523189}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523189} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bacc81c-a202-5de7-91a7-ef4e2100ffe9" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1682be06-115f-54ff-a73b-9b589617e8f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523105} {:answer/id #uuid "27fd6cae-d564-59e2-aa3f-8a705ed55e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523111}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523105} :answer-field/id #uuid "b680bc94-e35d-5672-8a29-61a6ce96c60b" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bb7d6994-e998-58f7-aa63-248113b6349d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=4 \\\\ -x &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9392a4b7-e0c1-50c1-a200-9aea19b85ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523152} {:answer/id #uuid "c54d1d3c-4700-5389-9521-819eca5efa3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523170} :answer-field/id #uuid "14a0dd8b-1651-52fe-a379-fa629f0b62ac" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc35ea2c-b5fa-5a21-af8c-52f26ca8f62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523166} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a8d720-eb68-5c11-a4f9-701068036d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523178}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523166} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f23ed57-d37c-5347-b6fc-2f6d63d7a37b" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fa07bf6-b3cb-5d2d-8a9f-a191e0b6e0f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523141} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a5ef39-054c-5b8e-b9af-e036a4693bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523171}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523141} :answer-field/id #uuid "c354c352-0b95-52ed-8029-4f2c45821f10" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec9855f3-8df8-5de8-aa96-4a294a867b64" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-3z &=5 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $z$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent dependent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "652676ed-c325-50b3-9370-c0907c671f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523136} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e7efd8-3b15-55b0-a40f-7c34b7c76512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523183} :answer-field/id #uuid "04645717-bac8-5e0f-80de-5dc8a6e34e04" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523093} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a148d48-fb64-5d16-b8f9-19a6596fe811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523096} {:answer/id #uuid "3abd678a-230b-520d-a0dd-63dc44fa005b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523096} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfcb9672-726a-595a-b7dd-19a4952a0aab" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fcc01c5-0bb3-5828-940a-30086cb2d945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523099} {:answer/id #uuid "d3e45317-561e-5c27-9374-58cfdb78546e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523174} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc3eaf4f-09ba-503b-a672-da707e643826" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fe67b029-391e-51be-a295-1e535d93c516" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -2x-4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is inconsistent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf30a48-c9e1-56ae-a6e7-d1c98a8ff3ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529217} {:answer/id #uuid "c73dcc5f-2dfd-545e-8686-1192c87baf69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529217} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c836807-d3ab-5654-828e-8cfc6899a48e" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3352e3a8-a31e-5489-b928-3600c98b31be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529215} {:answer/id #uuid "7eea3389-ae38-5700-acdf-02838bc43de5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529233}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529233} :answer-field/id #uuid "7319f1b7-7a37-5090-bc1d-79d9eee3c8d9" :answer-field/key "$det(Q)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59fb7559-abec-5a5a-8f38-66e0e05169a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529221} {:answer/id #uuid "edd1215a-893f-52eb-9b40-de5e574e65b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529249} :answer-field/id #uuid "885ed53f-bd5b-5462-9002-72b92ffeea39" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0f86b247-8f09-549d-8811-1a1520e150f7" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -1 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -1 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 2 & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & - \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{8 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2}- \\sqrt{2})+1(- \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{3})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}+4 \\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+1\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\  & =- \\frac{20}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$Q$ is a singular matrix” and $det(Q)=0$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "623acce1-fff7-50e6-838b-7b0788c7f4cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529223} {:answer/id #uuid "6f989a4f-56c1-50c2-8a6c-3fc3965f7ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529228}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529223} :answer-field/id #uuid "25dfb153-bf6c-5bc8-81b3-3f8c8e55fd75" :answer-field/key "$R$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ea2a503-d065-55b2-8fd1-d25f4f09f9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529227} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8e8b31-aab5-5ebf-9a6d-c0ce4e4dec83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529232}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529227} :answer-field/id #uuid "7227b94e-e860-5cf3-bd06-90e04b0b9867" :answer-field/key "$R$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529230} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0849452b-707f-5059-a47a-da630beb226a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529208} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6b1114-f6aa-5ce4-b2fd-bd99b174c462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529208} :answer-field/id #uuid "e852e547-0a05-5456-8b75-a7942f7d0613" :answer-field/key "$det(R)=\\frac{4}{5} - \\sqrt{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2eb19151-d434-5c12-a703-9c37eed13782" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{vmatrix}+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{vmatrix}+(- \\sqrt{2})\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)(- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{5}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5})+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)(- \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{4})+(- \\sqrt{2})(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}+\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot (- \\sqrt{2})+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{7}{4}+(- \\sqrt{2})\\cdot \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{5} \\\\  & =1- \\frac{7}{10}- \\frac{8}{5} \\\\  & =- \\frac{13}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(R)=- \\frac{13}{10}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement “$R$ is **not** a singular matrix” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f10ee21-6b89-5e0f-a04a-e49bcfa4c907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529218} {:answer/id #uuid "fe16b8a0-13d3-5554-8edd-ff60470da1a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529255}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529255} :answer-field/id #uuid "283cd5ed-404d-513a-8b29-74966f63a5de" :answer-field/key "$D$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bbf7977-41f6-5bb2-bc84-9b91b4aa2e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529239} {:answer/id #uuid "b655c0ce-1985-5548-8848-5fb9f83b43c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529242}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529239} :answer-field/id #uuid "57424796-2385-5961-a89c-2d74ee068fcd" :answer-field/key "$det(D)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "670467a6-e81c-5c99-be97-28f089cc9d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529225} {:answer/id #uuid "db4c2f01-affa-593d-9e86-c0393439ae7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529247} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbad6dc2-1046-5c88-93da-58012356da43" :answer-field/key "$D$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "58253580-dd5c-51ba-b42f-aea83256773d" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & - \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & - \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{vmatrix}+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{vmatrix}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & - \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}\\right)(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{10}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5})+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)(- \\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{3}{10})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}(\\frac{12 \\sqrt{2}}{25}- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{2}}{25}) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{2}}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{10}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{2}{5}\\right)\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\cdot \\frac{6 \\sqrt{2}}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}+\\frac{3}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=\\frac{6}{25}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement “$D$ is **not** a singular matrix” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87861eb3-5f89-51bb-a83b-a2a2f34426b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529234} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3191b2-823c-5ff2-9063-c65501bb4dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529252}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529252} :answer-field/id #uuid "0187374c-e9df-5d8a-b2e7-160b085f7e8a" :answer-field/key "$D$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e9331ae-3672-5960-a137-fec2b5ed94e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529222} {:answer/id #uuid "c78e9128-09e7-5dbd-8651-62e753136ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529245} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e0b79b6-ad2c-596a-b49a-2f831ec2b99d" :answer-field/key "$det(D)=\\frac{7}{40}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f014eef-cc68-5016-a321-04739726f29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529237} {:answer/id #uuid "9792a9f2-799d-58ba-9247-36ec66135b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529238}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529238} :answer-field/id #uuid "a28fbb07-9011-5ca0-97ac-fffd6b36f2ee" :answer-field/key "$D$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "71433954-37ca-5812-b277-05c8f0f0a4e4" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & 1 & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & 1 & - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\sqrt{7}\\end{vmatrix}+\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{4}\\right)\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{5} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}\\right)(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{8})+(-1)(- \\frac{7}{5}+\\frac{21}{20})+\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{4}\\right)(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{10}+\\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{10}) \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{8}+(-1)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{7}{20}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{7}}{4}\\right)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =- \\frac{7}{40}+\\frac{7}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=\\frac{7}{40}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$D$ is **not** a singular matrix” and $det(D)=\\frac{7}{40}$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13e93d6b-04f6-5d4f-b5b6-d410c07da27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529210} {:answer/id #uuid "ac318550-2f86-5de9-9b06-3ca0446a83ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529241}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529210} :answer-field/id #uuid "c469465a-d12b-5568-8d4c-567bbab54c8b" :answer-field/key "$det(N)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48843694-108e-5d14-bd01-367c88bbda7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529216} {:answer/id #uuid "66105f24-eeac-5dfa-906a-b29c7b525374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529224}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529216} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa6403a-374c-56a6-9e6e-eff87afdb677" :answer-field/key "$N$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529246} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0634ee5a-1fe4-5615-bb1f-de6045b61f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529207} {:answer/id #uuid "25008e01-79c7-58b7-aeed-e63a6324cfd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529211}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529211} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd12a97e-9c51-5ed4-8b7d-226953a0be67" :answer-field/key "$N$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f4817fa1-7160-5d08-adc7-564c3155c399" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $N$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nN=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 1 & 2 \\sqrt{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{3} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -2 & - 4 \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(N) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & 1 & 2 \\sqrt{2} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{3} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -2 & - 4 \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{1}{3} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -2 & - 4 \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & - 4 \\sqrt{2}\\end{vmatrix}+2 \\sqrt{2}\\begin{vmatrix}- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & - \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ - \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3} & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}(\\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{3}+2 \\sqrt{2})+(-1)(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{8}{3})+2 \\sqrt{2}(\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}- \\frac{4 \\sqrt{2}}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{10 \\sqrt{2}}{3}+(-1)\\cdot \\frac{16}{3}+2 \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{9}- \\frac{16}{3}+\\frac{8}{9} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(N)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$N$ is a singular matrix” and $det(N)=0$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 